.TH TIME 2
.SH NAME
time, ftime \- get date and time
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B "long time(0)"
.sp
.B "long time(tloc)"
.B "long *tloc;"
.sp
.B "#include <sys/types.h>"
.B "#include <sys/timeb.h>"
.B "ftime(tp)"
.B "struct timeb *tp;"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B time
returns the time since 00:00:00 GMT, Jan. 1, 1970, measured in
seconds.
.PP
If
.I tloc
is nonnull, the return value is also stored in the place to which
.I tloc
points.
.PP
The
.B ftime
entry fills in a structure pointed to by its argument, as defined
by
.BR <sys/timeb.h> :
.PP
.RS
.nf
.ta .7i
/*
 * Structure returned by ftime system call
 */
struct timeb {
	long time;
	unsigned int millitm;
	int timezone;
	int dstflag;
};
.fi
.RE
.PP
The structure contains the time since the epoch in seconds, up to 1000
milliseconds of more-precise interval, the local timezone (measured in
minutes of time westward from Greenwich), and a flag that, if nonzero,
indicates that daylight saving time applies locally during the appropriate
part of the year.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
date(1), stime(2), ctime(3)
.SH ASSEMBLER
(ftime = 35.)
.TP
PDP-11:
.nf
sys ftime; bufptr
.fi
.TP
8086:
.nf
BX = 35
AX = bufptr
int 0Xf1
.fi
.PP
(time = 13.; obsolete call)
.TP
PDP-11:
.nf
sys time
R0, R1 = time since 1970
.fi
.TP
8086:
.nf
BX = 13
int 0Xf1
AX, DX = time since 1970
.fi
.sp
